{"ts":"2026-08-30T20:58:12.273Z","author":"codex","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-5.6-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"ea5856882c73d923eca2015a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-5.6-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-web-jpa6"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GET graph installs or activates pm-graph and bypasses edit permission"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GET /api/projects/:projectId/pm/graph calls pmGraphExtensionGraphForProject, which calls ensureGraphExtension. The helper can install npm:pm-graph and activate it, so a safe-method request mutates project state. The pm router's permission middleware exempts GET/HEAD/OPTIONS, which also lets view-only collaborators trigger the mutation. This was found while tracing the complete CSRF boundary for pm-web-413z and must be repaired as a distinct route-semantics/authorization change."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":0},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["authorization","http-semantics","pm-graph","security"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-30T20:58:12.273Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-30T20:58:12.273Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"GET /pm/graph is observational and never installs, activates, or otherwise mutates an extension; any explicit provisioning uses a CSRF-protected unsafe method and requires edit permission; view-only users can read the fallback graph without changing project state; real route tests prove command logs remain mutation-free on GET."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"A state-changing GET can be triggered cross-origin and currently bypasses the edit-permission middleware by design."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reviewer","value":"security-review"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"pm-web 2026.8.29 at 7e09ca9"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Request GET /api/projects/:projectId/pm/graph for a project without active pm-graph; pmGraphExtensionGraphForProject calls ensureGraphExtension, which runs pm install and extension activate."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"GET reads the installed graph when available or returns the fallback graph without mutation."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"GET may install and activate pm-graph, including for view-only users."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.8.29"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"Graph HTTP routes"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/customer_impact","value":"Cross-origin or view-only callers can change a project's extension state through a nominally read-only endpoint."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/files","value":[{"path":"src/routes/pm.ts","scope":"project","note":"GET graph route and provisioning call"},{"path":"src/services/pm-runner.ts","scope":"project","note":"Mutating ensureGraphExtension helper"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"e0f8b8290a66cfd915e32e352d4fd6b73bd9be654bdad03677cd7bab305edac2","item_hash_version":2,"message":"Track state-changing graph GET discovered during CSRF boundary review","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
