{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-03T00:05:07.320Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"b01e10761a1f4fa3e8dc307a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.287","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-03T00:05:07.319Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","text":"Unblocked 2026-10-03 (cubic review on PR #161): this item's own acceptance is implemented in PR #161 (GET /pm/graph and neighbors are observational, provisioning needs an unsafe CSRF-protected method with edit permission, route tests assert mutation-free command logs). The 'blocked' status reflected repo-wide gates, not this defect: pm-web's whole-source coverage below 100 is tracked by pm-web-ulgy (routes/pm.ts and bootstrap) and pm-web-9ulj (route layer on real Postgres); extension-native response parity is pm-web-38n5. Close after PR #161 merges."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-03T00:05:07.320Z"}],"before_hash":"ca0858825e20c88652cdb6f10425e8bdcb2558f396bf68dde22f88cf7923d7b6","after_hash":"221cc09c4d319209441c63ca4a00237421490bfa2f20e876f158a8add1895438","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"34c7b5f4340eb4143b17b8c0bba195b4d8a1f4017b6f65c3a384297fc30ee96c"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-04T09:14:31.421Z","author":"pi-land-s2","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"458afb991196a5521f6e2e91","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-04T09:14:31.421Z","author":"pi-land-s2","text":"Accepted Greptile 4170831675: the 2026-10-03 comment claimed the graph route tests assert mutation-free command logs, but the test only checked the activation marker, extension install dir, and settings. The graph read test now records a real command log: PM_CLI_BIN wraps the real pm and appends every spawned argv, and the test asserts the log has no mutation entries after the GET/HEAD/owner/neighbors read phase. Red-first proof: with the GET route temporarily reverted to the provisioning behavior (and a no-op stub pm), the assertion fails on 'install npm:pm-graph --project' and 'extension activate pm-graph --project' per GET; with the shipped observational route it passes unchanged. This makes the item's command-log acceptance criterion actually verified."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-04T09:14:31.421Z"}],"before_hash":"221cc09c4d319209441c63ca4a00237421490bfa2f20e876f158a8add1895438","after_hash":"229575e4af3810873ed98a044ed7d2fc7d4cd203041cf383641098121847b025","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"3fa5f580717b5aeffc35a341ea327fae25bb46fb211b767432b4270f39f52156"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-04T10:14:37.361Z","author":"pi-land-s2","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"458afb991196a5521f6e2e91","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-04T10:14:37.361Z","author":"pi-land-s2","text":"Greptile follow-up 4176981023 on the command-log regression: accepted. The three new previous-env restores were declared after the t.after hook registration and after risky fixture setup, so an early failure (e.g. pm init) would read them in teardown from the temporal dead zone, masking the original error and skipping workspace removal. The captures now sit with previousRoot/previousMarker at the top of the test, before the hook and before any risky call, matching the file's established pattern. Focused graph test passes unchanged."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-04T10:14:37.361Z"}],"before_hash":"229575e4af3810873ed98a044ed7d2fc7d4cd203041cf383641098121847b025","after_hash":"5a18dbf90e73a603a7f6e0ecb9ed252e739c7f3e494d3c828f651a4e6b036be7","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"fa329e5b58add788b9cd85e82b896526fdfd6dfa0aa4f049ba583ef947fc266f"}
